{"authored" [{"question" "q-89054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $G$ be the event that the chosen student obtained the top grade, and let $A$ be the event that the student is from Group $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the student is from Group $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student obtained the top grade, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $35%$ of her students are in Group $A$ and $65%$ are in Group $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.35,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.65.\n$$\n\n- Since $20%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=0.20.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top  grade is $0.265,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=0.265.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.265 & =(0.20)(0.35)+P(G|{A}^{′})(0.65) \\\\ 0.265 & =0.07+0.65P(G|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.65P(G|{A}^{′}) & =0.195 \\\\ P(G|{A}^{′}) & =0.30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected student from Group $B$ obtained the top grade is $0.30.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7157bfba2b1ae2dc481e0a1e2123c68f7ada1e1612ecfbab4c6cac1341ed857" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.25"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.30"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.35"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.40"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.45"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/state.json" "file_sha256" "20bd7c95ad82250427a448e4c8af2649985eff66f744a5b9ae03a24e61c05639" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A certain disease is present in $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ of the population. A test to detect the disease gives a positive result in $\\dfrac{10}{11}$ of the people with the disease, and $\\dfrac{3}{11}$ of the people without the disease. What is the probability that a randomly selected patient tests positive for the disease?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/example-7862.json" "file_sha256" "5614f43c8087d9ea8012ab5c6100409fac12d94a624490d6221d3780d3d7d8d8" "basis" 557 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948571/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-122306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a class, $20$ students are boys, and $24$ are girls. $5%$ of the boys are engaged in a sports section, and $25%$ of the girls are engaged in a sports section. What is the probability that a randomly selected student is engaged in a sports section?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $S$ be the event that the selected student is engaged in a sports section, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student is engaged in a sports section, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S\\cap B)+P(S\\cap {B}^{′})\n$$\n\nThere are $20$ boys in the class, and $5%$ of them are engaged in a sports section. So, the number of boys engaged in a sports section is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{100}\\cdot 20=1.\n$$\n\nThere are $24$  girls in the class, and $25%$ of them are engaged in a sports section. So, the number of girls  engaged in a sports section is\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}\\cdot 24=6.\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(S\\cap B),$ we take the number of boys engaged in a sports section $(1)$ and divide it by the total number of students in the class $(20+24=44).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{44}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(S\\cap {B}^{′}),$ we take the number of girls engaged in a sports section $(6)$ and divide it by the total number of students in the class $(44).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap {B}^{′})=\\frac{6}{44}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student is engaged in a sports section is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S\\cap B)+P(S\\cap {B}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{44}+\\frac{6}{44} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{44}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-122306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{22}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{44}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{44}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{44}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{44}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{44}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a class, $17$ students are boys, and $23$ are girls. Of the boys, $2$ belong to the school chess club. Of the girls, $3$ are in the chess club. What is the probability that a randomly selected student in the class is in the chess club?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen student is on the chess club, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student is on the chess club, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C\\cap B)+P(C\\cap {B}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(C\\cap B),$ we take the number of students in the class who are on the chess club and are boys $(2)$ and divide by the total number of students in the class $(17+23=40).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap B)=\\frac{2}{40}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(C\\cap {B}^{′}),$ we take the number of students in the class who are on the chess club and are girls $(3)$ and divide by the total number of students in the class $(40).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap {B}^{′})=\\frac{3}{40}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student is on the chess club is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C\\cap B)+P(C\\cap {B}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{40}+\\frac{3}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-88830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A gas station offers two types of gasoline, regular and premium. On a certain day, of the $43$ customers who bought regular gas, $23$ paid with a credit card. On the same day, of the $38$ customers that bought premium gas, $31$ of them paid with a credit card. What is the probability of a randomly selected customer paying with a credit card?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen person paid with a credit card, and let $R$ be the event that the person bought regular gas. Then ${R}^{′}$ is the event that the person bought premium gas.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person paid with a credit card, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C\\cap R)+P(C\\cap {R}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(C\\cap R),$ we take the number of people who bought regular gas and paid with a credit card $(23)$ and divide by the total number of customers on that day $(43+38=81).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap R)=\\frac{23}{81}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(C\\cap {R}^{′}),$ we take the number of people who bought premium gas and paid with a credit card $(31)$ and divide by the total number of customers on that day $(81).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap {R}^{′})=\\frac{31}{81}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person paid with a credit card is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C\\cap R)+P(C\\cap {R}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{81}+\\frac{31}{81} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{81} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-88922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Alice has two email accounts, $A$ and $B.$ In account $A,$ she received $24$ emails of which $5$ are spam. In the account $B,$ she received $18$ emails of which $2$ are spam. What is the probability that a randomly selected email in either account is spam?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen email is spam, and let $A$ be the event that the email was received in account $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the email was received in account $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected email is spam, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S\\cap A)+P(S\\cap {A}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(S\\cap A),$ we take the number of emails in account A that are spam $(5)$ and divide by the total number of emails received $(24+18=42).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap A)=\\frac{5}{42}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(S\\cap {A}^{′}),$ we take the number of emails in account $B$ that are spam $(2)$ and divide by the total number of emails received $(24+18=42).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap {A}^{′})=\\frac{2}{42}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected email is spam is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S\\cap A)+P(S\\cap {A}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{42}+\\frac{2}{42} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{42} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-88892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Among the people arrested in a certain city in the mid-1990s, $18%$ were males under $18$ years old and $54%$ were males of $18$ years old and over. What is the probability that a person selected at random from all those arrested is a male?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $M$ be the event that the chosen person is a male, and let $U$ be the event that the chosen person is under $18.$ Then, ${U}^{′}$ is the event that the person is $18$ or over.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person is a male, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap U)+P(M\\cap {U}^{′})\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap U)=0.18,\\,P(M\\cap {U}^{′})=0.54.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person is a male is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap U)+P(M\\cap {U}^{′}) \\\\  & =0.18+0.54 \\\\  & =0.72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-122397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.12"] ["math" "0.18"] ["math" "0.54"] ["math" "0.62"] ["math" "0.72"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.72"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A certain disease is present in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the population. A test to detect the disease gives a positive result in $\\frac{9}{10}$ of the people with the disease and in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the people without the disease. What is the probability that a randomly selected patient tests positive for the disease?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $A$ be the event that the test is positive for the selected patient, and let $D$ be the event that the patient has the disease. Then, ${D}^{′}$ is the event that the patient does not have the disease.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected patient gives a positive result, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(A|D)P(D)+P(A|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the disease is present in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the population, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=\\frac{1}{10},\\,P({D}^{′})=\\frac{9}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Since the test gives a positive result in $\\frac{9}{10}$ of the people with the disease, and in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the people without the disease, we have\n\n$$\nP(A|D)=\\frac{9}{10},\\,P(A|{D}^{′})=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected patient tests positive for the disease is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =P(A|D)P(D)+P(A|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{9}{10})(\\frac{1}{10})+(\\frac{1}{10})(\\frac{9}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{100}+\\frac{9}{100} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{100} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-89031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{100}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{50}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{50}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Sophia has two email accounts, account $A$ and account $B.$ She receives $35%$ of her emails in account $A,$ and the remaining $65%$ go into account $B.$ Approximately $15%$ of the emails received in account $A$ are spam while $25%$ of the emails received in account $B$ are spam. What is the probability that a randomly selected email is spam?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen email is spam, and let $A$ be the event that the email selected is from account $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the email selected is from account $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected email is spam, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S|A)P(A)+P(S|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $35%$ of the emails are received in account $A$ and the remaining $65%$ in account $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.35,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.65.\n$$\n\n- Since $15%$ of the emails received in account $A$ are spam while $25%$ of the emails received in account $B$ are spam, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|A)=0.15,\\,P(S|{A}^{′})=0.25.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected email is spam is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S|A)P(A)+P(S|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.15)(0.35)+(0.25)(0.65) \\\\  & =0.215.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-88980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.215"] ["math" "0.251"] ["math" "0.315"] ["math" "0.521"] ["math" "0.715"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.215"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A math teacher split their calculus class into two groups, Group $A$ and Group $B.$ Group $A$ has $43%$ of the total number of students, while Group $B$ has $57%$ of the total number of students. If $23%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, and $19%$ of the students in Group $B$ obtained the top grade, what is the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top grade?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $G$ be the event that the chosen student obtained the top grade, and let $A$ be the event that the student is from Group $A.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the student is from Group $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student obtained the top grade, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $43%$ of their students are in Group $A$ and $57%$ are in Group $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.43,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.57.\n$$\n\n- Since $23%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade and $19%$ of the students in Group $B$ obtained the top grade, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=0.23,\\,P(G|{A}^{′})=0.19.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top grade\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.23)(0.43)+(0.19)(0.57) \\\\  & ≈0.207\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-89041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.197"] ["math" "0.207"] ["math" "0.213"] ["math" "0.227"] ["math" "0.312"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.207"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a class, $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the students are boys, and $\\frac{2}{3}$ are girls. Of the boys, $\\frac{1}{6}$ of them play soccer, and of the girls, $\\frac{1}{4}$ of them play soccer. What is the probability that a randomly selected student plays soccer?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen student plays soccer, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student plays soccer, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S|B)P(B)+P(S|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the students are boys and $\\frac{2}{3}$ are girls, we have\n\n$$\nP(B)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,P({B}^{′})=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the boys play soccer and $\\frac{1}{4}$ of the girls play soccer, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|B)=\\frac{1}{6},\\,P(S|{B}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student plays soccer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S|B)P(B)+P(S|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{1}{4})(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-88578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{24}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A student answers a multiple-choice test. Each question of the test has four possible answers, and only one choice is correct. The student knows the correct answer for $60%$ of the questions. If the student decides to select an answer at random for the questions that she does not know the answer to, what is the probability that a randomly selected question on the test is correct?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C$ be the event that the selected question is correct, and let $K$ be the event that the student knew the answer. Then ${K}^{′}$ is the event that the student did not know the answer.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected question is correct, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|K)P(K)+P(C|{K}^{′})P({K}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the student knows the answer to $60%$ of the questions, we have\n\n$$\nP(K)=0.6,\\,P({K}^{′})=0.4.\n$$\n\n- Since each question has four possible answers, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|K)=1,\\,P(C|{K}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}=0.25.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected question on the test is correct is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|K)P(K)+P(C|{K}^{′})P({K}^{′}) \\\\  & =(1)(0.6)+(0.25)(0.4) \\\\  & =0.6+0.1 \\\\  & =0.70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-88977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.65"] ["math" "0.68"] ["math" "0.70"] ["math" "0.72"] ["math" "0.75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-88977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.70"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Company $A$ supplies $80%$ of widgets for a car shop and only $1%$ of their widgets turn out to be defective. Company $B$ supplies the remaining $20%$ of widgets. The probability that a widget from the car shop will be defective is $0.014.$ If a customer randomly purchases a widget supplied by company $B,$ what is the probability that it will be defective?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $D$ be the event that a widget will be defective, and let $A$ be the event that the widget is supplied by company $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the widget is supplied by company $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly purchased widget will be defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since company $A$ supplies $80%$ of widgets for a car shop and company $B$ the remaining $20%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.80,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.20.\n$$\n\n- Since $1%$ of the widget supplied by company $A$ are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.01.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a widget from the car shop is defective will be $0.014,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.014.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.014 & =(0.01)(0.80)+P(D|{A}^{′})(0.20) \\\\ 0.014 & =0.008+0.20P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.20P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.006 \\\\ P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected widget supplied by company $B$ will be defective is $0.03.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-122412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.03"] ["math" "0.05"] ["math" "0.13"] ["math" "0.23"] ["math" "0.3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.03"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a gas station, $55%$ of the customers buy regular gasoline while $45%$ buy premium gasoline. If $60%$ of the customers that buy regular gasoline usually pay with a credit card and the probability that a randomly selected customer pays with a credit card is $0.645,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected customer who buys premium gasoline usually pays with a credit card? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen person pays with a credit card, and let $R$ be the event that the person buys regular gas. Then ${R}^{′}$ is the event that the person buys premium gas.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person pays with a credit card, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $55%$ of the customers buy regular gasoline while $45%$ buy premium gasoline, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.55,\\,P({R}^{′})=0.45.\n$$\n\n- Since $60%$ of the customers that buy regular gasoline pay with a credit card, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|R)=0.60.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected customer pays with a credit card is $0.645,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(C)=0.645.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(C|{R}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′}) \\\\ 0.645 & =(0.60)(0.55)+P(C|{R}^{′})(0.45) \\\\ 0.645 & =0.33+0.45P(C|{R}^{′}) \\\\ 0.45P(C|{R}^{′}) & =0.315 \\\\ P(C|{R}^{′}) & =0.70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected customer who buys premium gasoline usually pays with a credit card is $0.70.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-89053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.60"] ["math" "0.65"] ["math" "0.70"] ["math" "0.75"] ["math" "0.80"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.70"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the total components manufactured, $60%$ of them are produced by machine $A,$ and the remaining $40%$ are produced by machine $B.$ Of the components produced by machine $A,$ $10%$ are defective. In total, $12%$ of all components produced are defective. If a component produced by machine $B$ is selected at random, what is the probability of it being defective? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $D$ be the event that the selected component is defective, and let $A$ be the event that the component was produced by machine $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the component was produced by machine $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since machine $A$ produces $60%$ of the components and $B$ the remaining $40%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.60,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.40.\n$$\n\n- Since $10%$ of the components produced by machine $A$ are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.10.\n$$\n\n- Since $12%$ of the components produced are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.12 & =(0.10)(0.60)+P(D|{A}^{′})(0.40) \\\\ 0.12 & =0.06+0.40P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.40P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.06 \\\\ P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected component produced by machine $B$ is defective is $0.15.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-89042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.12"] ["math" "0.15"] ["math" "0.17"] ["math" "0.20"] ["math" "0.25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Two machines ${M}_{1}$ and ${M}_{2}$ in a particular factory produce $75%$ and $25%,$ respectively, of the total daily output of electronic tubes. It is known that $4%$ of the tubes produced by ${M}_{1}$ are defective and that the probability that a randomly selected tube from a day's production is defective is $0.0375.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected tube produced by ${M}_{2}$ is defective?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected tube is defective, and let $A$ be the event that the tube is produced by machine ${M}_{1}.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the tube is produced by machine ${M}_{2}.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected tube from a day's production is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since machine ${M}_{1}$ produces $75%$ of the total daily output of electronic tubes and ${M}_{2}$ the remaining $25%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.75,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.25.\n$$\n\n- Since $4%$ of the tubes produced by machine ${M}_{1}$ are defective,  we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.04.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected tube from a day's production is defective is $0.0375,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.0375.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.0375 & =(0.04)(0.75)+P(D|{A}^{′})(0.25) \\\\ 0.0375 & =0.03+0.25P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.0075 & =0.25P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected tube produced by ${M}_{2}$ is defective is $0.03.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-122403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.03"] ["math" "0.08"] ["math" "0.10"] ["math" "0.15"] ["math" "0.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-122403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.03"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A math teacher splits her calculus class into two groups, Group $A$ and Group $B.$ Of the total students, $35%$ of her students are in Group $A,$ and $65%$ are in Group $B.$ If $20%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, and the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top grade is $0.265,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected student from Group $B$ obtained the top grade? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $G$ be the event that the chosen student obtained the top grade, and let $A$ be the event that the student is from Group $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the student is from Group $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student obtained the top grade, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $35%$ of her students are in Group $A$ and $65%$ are in Group $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.35,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.65.\n$$\n\n- Since $20%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=0.20.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top  grade is $0.265,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=0.265.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.265 & =(0.20)(0.35)+P(G|{A}^{′})(0.65) \\\\ 0.265 & =0.07+0.65P(G|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.65P(G|{A}^{′}) & =0.195 \\\\ P(G|{A}^{′}) & =0.30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected student from Group $B$ obtained the top grade is $0.30.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b63c4c5df2be6186b2681866b74e6dbc0f63ea32c90560f3fb50340a14db892"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a96566558a9054770e61876ebdaa977772882929b15a0bdebbf0d6d7d7be8e5"} {"question" "q-89054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.25"] ["math" "0.30"] ["math" "0.35"] ["math" "0.40"] ["math" "0.45"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cours